maintained-in-repo: yes
refreshed-by:       nothing — edit main/server.cfg directly and commit

Unlike the other seeds, this one is not tracked from an upstream repository and
tools/refresh-seeds.sh does not touch it. It is a single server.cfg, so pinning
a commit and pruning a checkout would add machinery with no upstream to drift
from.

Originally adapted from https://github.com/matracey/docker-cod4 (server.cfg, no
declared license). Plutainer changes: the shipped placeholder rcon_password
"my_rcon_password" is blanked — a known credential in a published image is worth
nothing to the operator and plenty to anyone scanning for servers. Set one with
PLUTAINER_RCON_PASSWORD or by editing app/configs/server.cfg.
